														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4244323">
									

<p>I like this but also i feel like the focus of SCP-4184 being &quot;the booklet the music is written in&quot; instead of the song itself feels weird? Like it seems to me that it's the actual piece of music that has the anomalous effect and not the booklet; which means that a mention of either researchers or a foundation AI looking out for other instances in the containment section could be cool. If you're wanting to go down the route of it being a thing dependent on the booklet, it might be worth adding some testing procedures indicating that e.g, there's a pianist unfamiliar with the piece playing it straight from the booklet?</p>
<p>It might also be interesting to play around with e.g, does it work on recordings of the song? Does it have to be played live? what about parts of the song or if the song is distorted? It's not exactly clear from the logs how the music is played which feels needlessly imprecise to me.</p>
<p>The research logs feel,,,excessive to me? They add a lot of emotional impact to the SCP sure, but from a research perspective, it's not exactly clear why the testing was carried out or what the foundation hoped to achieve from it?</p>

							</div>

								
					
